    {
      "id": "holt_godfrey_wall",
      "cell": [
        0,
        16
      ],
      "kind": "book",
      "label": "Writing on the wall",
      "model": "drawings",
      "codex": "godfrey_list",
      "flag": "godfrey_list_read",
      "text": "The whole wall is covered in charcoal, floor to as high as a tall man can reach, in a big careful hand. Names, and after each one a few words. Sir Teodor: pears, and his grey mare. Sir Bastian: arguing. Dame Ilona: her son, who lived. Sir Mattias: songs he got wrong on purpose. Hundreds more. Near the bottom, smudged and gone over many times: Godfrey: Gwenllian, who laughed like a goose. The light. The oath. Remember the oath."
    },
    {
      "id": "holt_godfrey_cot",
